faq:
  - q: What is family therapy?
    a: Family therapy is a form of psychotherapy in which family members work together with a psychologist to strengthen relationships and improve communication dynamics.
  - q: Who should attend family therapy?
    a: All family members or those directly involved in the issue may attend. The psychologist will help you decide who should participate at the initial assessment.
  - q: When is family therapy most helpful?
    a: Family conflict, communication breakdown, parent-child tension, bereavement or major life changes are situations where family therapy provides effective support.
